<!-- Fork: the "add a note" glyph, shown on main-list rows that carry no note
     yet. The plus is drawn deliberately large — it fills most of the page below
     the folded corner — because at row size a Material-proportioned plus is
     indistinguishable from the plain note glyph (ic_note_24dp), and this one has
     to read as an ADD control. evenOdd makes the plus and the fold notch holes
     in the page. No android:tint, so RowPills' runtime tint (the fork theme
     colour, at the add affordance's lower alpha) is the single source of tint. -->
